WEBVTT

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:10.480
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:12.650
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:16.160
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.900
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:33.710
Mr. Grizzly's Reunion.

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:41.680
Hello?

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:45.290
We are currently conducting 
a phone survey.

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:49.410
Please give your answers after 
the automated questions.

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:53.810
Have you been suffering 
from a lack of sleep lately?

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:55.800
I know it's you, Polar Bear!

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:58.340
*Note: 
Voice Changer

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:58.020
Was it that obvious?

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:02.510
You just woke up recently, 
and you're asleep again?

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:05.530
Yeah, I went back
 to bed to hibernate.

00:02:05.970 --> 00:02:07.440
Not just back.

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:08.690
What?

00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:11.390
You've gone back about eight times.

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:13.980
Because you keep waking me up!

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.660
Let me sleep, damn it!

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:19.740
Hibernating

00:02:30.130 --> 00:02:31.610
Polar Bear...

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:35.920
You really need to...

00:02:36.910 --> 00:02:38.740
...stop that, damn it!

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:44.100
It's been a while.

00:02:45.550 --> 00:02:46.680
Mom...

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:51.520
You really need to stop 
with the harsh speech.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:54.160
Here, I brought you a gift.

00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:59.610
I-I always tell you to let 
me know when you're coming.

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:01.660
Even though you were hibernating?

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:05.670
I thought I'd surprise you.

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:08.910
Here you go, Little Grizz.

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:12.470
I asked you not to call 
me that anymore.

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:17.880
Maple syrup and Alaskan salmon!

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:19.430
Thanks!

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:27.250
When'd you get back?

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:29.390
On the last flight yesterday.

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:32.780
Being at home really is relaxing.

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:35.360
Maybe I'll move back in.

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:39.080
Please. You were the one 
who moved overseas,

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:43.090
so you could have a LOHAS-style 
county life where grandpa was born.

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:49.680
Well? How does the authentic 
maple syrup taste?

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:52.870
It's fresh from this spring.

00:03:53.910 --> 00:03:56.340
So good...

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:01.310
Oh? It looks like you've 
got a visitor.

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:05.300
Oh, don't worry about 
it, Mom. I'll get it.

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:13.470
Damn it, Polar Bear!

00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:16.440
Certain 
Victory

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:16.440
Polar Bear <i>(shirokuma)</i>?

00:04:16.510 --> 00:04:20.900
That's Hiroshima! 
What are you up to <i>(nanimon)</i>?!

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:24.540
That's a traditional variety act <i>(iromon)</i>!

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:28.870
That's an Iga ninja <i>(iga mono)</i>!

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:32.830
And this is for hot pot <i>(nabemono)</i>!

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:37.290
Hello, Polar Bear.

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:39.010
Oh, hello.

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:41.220
It's been a very long time.

00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:49.110
The cherry blossom viewing 
train is coming through!

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:50.180
Through...

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:52.640
Since it's spring already,

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:56.100
I made it meunière
 instead of in a hot pot.

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:58.720
My, it looks delicious.

00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:02.980
Are you sure we can have some, as well?

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:05.770
Please, eat up.

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:06.940
Well, then...

00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:11.590
It's delicious!

00:05:11.590 --> 00:05:14.790
Nothing better than getting fish 
fresh from its natural habitat.

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:20.120
But, my, you seem rather young 
to be Mr. Grizzly's mother.

00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:22.730
Now that you mention it...

00:05:23.180 --> 00:05:25.470
I hope you don't mind me 
asking, but how old are you?

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:28.430
Oh? Well, this year...

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:29.980
I'm seventeen.

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:31.930
Seventeen?

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:35.010
What? You don't look it at all!

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:37.230
You're older than me?

00:05:39.470 --> 00:05:40.610
Well, I am a bear.

00:05:41.110 --> 00:05:44.470
Your fur is so sleek and youthful!

00:05:44.470 --> 00:05:47.570
Could you tell me your secret 
behind your cuticles?

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:51.030
Oh, I don't do anything 
special, really.

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:54.620
What's the matter, Ms. Tanaka?

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:58.180
Oh... It's just I'm the oldest...

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:01.620
Nice to meet you. I'm Penguin.

00:06:02.430 --> 00:06:03.590
I'm Panda.

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:07.220
I'm always taking care of Mr. Grizzly.

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:11.140
No, you mean that he's always 
taking care of you...

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:14.530
Nice to meet you. 
I'm Little Grizz's mother.

00:06:14.530 --> 00:06:15.740
Little Grizz?

00:06:18.760 --> 00:06:21.550
Mom! Don't call me that!

00:06:21.550 --> 00:06:22.680
"Little Grizz"?

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:26.100
Oh, I see. "Little Grizz."

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:31.580
All passengers please hurry on board.

00:06:31.580 --> 00:06:33.310
Board...

00:06:34.420 --> 00:06:36.590
All aboard!

00:06:36.590 --> 00:06:37.920
Express!

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:47.340
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:49.980
We'll come again.

00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:51.520
Thank you for the food.

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:53.860
Bye!

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:53.860
See you later!

00:06:54.230 --> 00:06:58.150
Well, I'm going to the bar, 
so you can head home.

00:06:54.230 --> 00:06:58.150
Bye!

00:06:58.390 --> 00:06:59.270
All right.

00:06:58.390 --> 00:07:00.000
See you later!

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.880
Do your best at work.

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:02.960
Yeah.

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:08.330
Jeez... This is totally 
throwing things off.

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:14.280
Guess I'll knock a few 
out before I head in.

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:24.720
Man, that felt great!

00:07:25.980 --> 00:07:28.720
Sorry to leave you 
with the bar, Otter.

00:07:30.210 --> 00:07:31.600
Thanks for waiting.

00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:33.990
Here's your bourbon.

00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:36.020
Thanks, Ma'am.

00:07:36.920 --> 00:07:39.060
Mom! Why are you here?!

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:41.380
Well? How do I look?

00:07:43.210 --> 00:07:45.420
What the hell, Otter?

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:48.040
She's been a lot of help.

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:50.530
I heard you're not sleeping well.

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:53.340
She's an amazing mom

00:07:53.850 --> 00:07:55.740
to help you with the bar.

00:07:56.140 --> 00:07:59.290
These fuki bud spring rolls are delicious.

00:07:59.850 --> 00:08:01.080
Fuki buds?!

00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:03.960
The inari and roll sushi plate
 is great, too.

00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:05.750
Inari and roll sushi plate?!

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:07.680
Could I get another miso soup?

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:09.710
Miso soup?!

00:08:10.430 --> 00:08:12.680
Not just any miso soup...

00:08:13.980 --> 00:08:15.340
It's a mother's cooking.

00:08:26.210 --> 00:08:28.570
Mom!

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:34.990
Who asked you to make 
healthy family cooking?

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:37.890
This ain't a small restaurant!

00:08:46.820 --> 00:08:48.130
I'm sorry.

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:53.880
Well, the bar keep is back, 
so I'll head home.

00:08:54.270 --> 00:08:59.850
Everyone, please keep 
visiting Grizzly's Bar.

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:12.200
Bar keep.

00:09:13.170 --> 00:09:14.280
What?

00:09:16.830 --> 00:09:18.370
Have a taste.

00:09:32.050 --> 00:09:32.800
See?

00:09:33.850 --> 00:09:34.830
It's good, ain't it?

00:09:40.590 --> 00:09:42.440
Hey, wait a sec!

00:09:43.330 --> 00:09:44.290
Mom!

00:09:46.070 --> 00:09:48.480
This is pretty good.

00:09:50.630 --> 00:09:53.510
This isn't bad once in a while.

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:54.900
Got that right.

00:09:55.630 --> 00:09:58.360
Could I get another gin lime?

00:09:58.880 --> 00:09:59.770
Sure.

00:09:59.770 --> 00:10:02.840
These ginger sardines are fantastic.

00:10:03.150 --> 00:10:04.830
Thank you very much.

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:09.050
The Japanese style omelettes 
are wonderful, too.

00:10:09.050 --> 00:10:13.010
Bar keep, this is the owner of the 
bakery I'm training at, Ms. Donkey.

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:15.240
Nice to meet you.

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:17.050
Welcome.

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:21.490
Why don't we try to make a Japanese 
style bakery dish with these?

00:10:21.490 --> 00:10:25.560
Japanese style omelette 
sandwiches? Sounds great.

00:10:26.530 --> 00:10:27.930
Little Grizz!

00:10:29.450 --> 00:10:31.000
Could I get another scotch?

00:10:31.430 --> 00:10:33.540
Could I get another 
Shandygaff, Little Grizz?

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:36.240
I want bamboo grass 
juice, Little Grizz.

00:10:36.930 --> 00:10:38.530
Why you...

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:41.010
Could I get a Kahlua 
milk, Little Grizz?

00:10:41.010 --> 00:10:42.310
Even you, Sasako?!

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:46.070
Damn it. Looks like I have no choice.

00:10:46.070 --> 00:10:48.220
Tequila, Little Grizz.

00:10:48.220 --> 00:10:49.640
I ain't going to let you 
get away with that!

00:10:49.640 --> 00:10:50.670
Why?!

00:11:15.190 --> 00:11:17.510
My name ain't Little Grizz...

00:11:47.930 --> 00:11:50.300
Good night, Little Grizz.

00:11:56.940 --> 00:12:01.900
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:11:57.870 --> 00:12:00.470
Mr. Llama's Time Capsule.

00:12:02.520 --> 00:12:05.390
What? A time capsule?

00:12:05.390 --> 00:12:05.890
Yes.

00:12:06.520 --> 00:12:09.290
I sent a letter to myself years ago, 
and it just arrived.

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:12.290
Under the 
Japanese Cedar

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:12.290
School

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:12.290
Treasure Map!

00:12:10.100 --> 00:12:12.290
Wow! The Mononoke Forest!

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:14.650
You left a time capsule there?

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:15.710
Yes.

00:12:16.690 --> 00:12:18.750
How does Miss Sasako know about this?

00:12:19.290 --> 00:12:21.320
Long, long ago...

00:12:21.320 --> 00:12:26.000
Miss Sasako and Mr. Llama 
lived in the same city.

00:12:26.910 --> 00:12:28.760
Why are you saying it 
like an old folktale?

00:12:29.250 --> 00:12:30.720
Little boy...

00:12:29.570 --> 00:12:30.720
Let's not sing the song!

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:35.030
I got it! "Manga Japanese Folkta—"

00:12:35.030 --> 00:12:37.110
This isn't a song intro quiz!

00:12:37.680 --> 00:12:40.060
What did you bury, Mr. Llama?

00:12:40.460 --> 00:12:42.750
The thing is, I don't remember at all.

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:47.120
I'm going to go dig it up tomorrow, 
so it'll be exciting.

00:12:53.840 --> 00:12:56.400
What about the café, Mr. Polar Bear?

00:12:57.000 --> 00:13:01.710
Don't worry. The Café's other 
name is the Fickle Café.

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:04.820
That's not a good fickle!

00:13:06.740 --> 00:13:09.700
You've turned micro, Miss Sasako.

00:13:10.190 --> 00:13:13.160
I guess shortened it'd 
be Micro Miss Sasako.

00:13:13.160 --> 00:13:14.640
That's not shortened, at all.

00:13:15.130 --> 00:13:16.670
I'm Micro Sasako.

00:13:17.210 --> 00:13:20.020
Could you stop that, Mr. Penguin?

00:13:20.420 --> 00:13:23.900
Why? Even though I stayed 
up all night making it?

00:13:24.270 --> 00:13:27.390
Wow! Talk about cramming!

00:13:27.760 --> 00:13:29.580
That's not really a compliment.

00:13:30.360 --> 00:13:32.290
I'm here...

00:13:32.920 --> 00:13:35.250
too...

00:13:37.780 --> 00:13:38.600
Count-off.

00:13:39.060 --> 00:13:39.670
One.

00:13:40.150 --> 00:13:40.930
Two.

00:13:40.930 --> 00:13:41.380
Three.

00:13:42.260 --> 00:13:42.960
Four!

00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:44.960
Five...

00:13:44.960 --> 00:13:46.950
So the five of us are all here.

00:13:48.930 --> 00:13:51.350
Oh? Where's Panda?

00:13:51.980 --> 00:13:54.220
So cute!

00:13:55.090 --> 00:13:57.570
It's rare to see a panda 
sleeping in the luggage rack.

00:13:57.570 --> 00:13:59.300
I'm totally uploading this to my blog!

00:14:01.430 --> 00:14:03.210
Searches for "Panda sleeping 
in the luggage rack"

00:14:03.210 --> 00:14:05.610
is are spiking across the Internet.

00:14:06.500 --> 00:14:10.080
I'll go fetch Panda with Mr. Penguin,

00:14:10.080 --> 00:14:12.040
so go on ahead with Mr. Llama.

00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:13.800
Right...

00:14:13.800 --> 00:14:15.000
All right, Mr. Llama...

00:14:19.320 --> 00:14:21.930
How about a llama sleeping 
under a bench?

00:14:24.010 --> 00:14:27.090
Well, I guess I'll take one
to remember it by.

00:14:28.550 --> 00:14:30.490
Hits
568,108

00:14:28.550 --> 00:14:30.490
Popular Photo
"Panda sleeping in the luggage rack"

00:14:28.550 --> 00:14:33.390
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:14:30.490 --> 00:14:33.390
Plain Photo
"Llama sleeping under a bench"

00:14:30.490 --> 00:14:33.390
Hits
32

00:14:37.950 --> 00:14:39.710
It's so nostalgic.

00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:41.150
Indeed.

00:14:45.120 --> 00:14:46.720
The Asunaro Bakery!

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:51.520
Looks like the cream bread

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:54.930
is still shaped like a leaf.

00:14:56.020 --> 00:14:58.830
Since we're here, 
how about we buy five of them?

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:00.580
Five of them?

00:15:01.510 --> 00:15:02.800
Enough for everyone!

00:15:03.090 --> 00:15:05.920
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:11.050
Suginoko Park

00:15:12.040 --> 00:15:14.820
So the swings were this small...

00:15:15.710 --> 00:15:18.680
I used to be able to sit on it 
 without any problem, too.

00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:21.970
How did you sit on it?

00:15:24.970 --> 00:15:27.020
I'll leave that up to 
your imagination.

00:15:31.000 --> 00:15:34.220
Wow, that's amazing, Mr. Llama!

00:15:36.420 --> 00:15:38.870
Did you always like sandboxes?

00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:39.620
Yes.

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:45.590
My goal one day is to make 
the Sagrada Família.

00:15:45.990 --> 00:15:47.060
I see...

00:15:50.520 --> 00:15:52.010
Ms. Raccoon!

00:15:53.440 --> 00:15:54.710
It's me, Sasako!

00:15:57.120 --> 00:15:57.970
Oh!

00:15:58.470 --> 00:16:00.510
The one that lived behind Hama no Yu.

00:16:00.510 --> 00:16:01.160
Yes.

00:16:01.770 --> 00:16:04.490
Sasako who was 
famous for getting lost!

00:16:05.310 --> 00:16:06.150
Yes...

00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:10.750
Didn't you end up going 
over to the next city

00:16:10.750 --> 00:16:13.170
because you wanted to see the 
wind station's turbine up close?

00:16:13.170 --> 00:16:14.060
Yes...

00:16:16.260 --> 00:16:17.350
How ya been?

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:19.960
You've always had a 
habit of wandering off

00:16:19.960 --> 00:16:22.310
so I always worried about you.

00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:24.830
Yes... I'm doing okay.

00:16:25.250 --> 00:16:27.070
Hello, it's been a while.

00:16:27.950 --> 00:16:28.870
Who are you?

00:16:29.600 --> 00:16:31.800
I'm Llama, the one you'd

00:16:32.800 --> 00:16:35.120
always yell at and make help you clean.

00:16:35.510 --> 00:16:36.910
Oh, the little troublemaker!

00:16:37.290 --> 00:16:37.920
Yes.

00:16:39.510 --> 00:16:41.040
It's been a while.

00:16:41.040 --> 00:16:44.010
Well, haven't you calmed down a bit?

00:16:44.010 --> 00:16:46.560
I may not look it, 
but I'm an adult now.

00:16:46.870 --> 00:16:51.550
But you've calmed down so much, 
you look rather dull now.

00:16:58.270 --> 00:17:01.560
Ms. Raccoon's sharp 
tongue hasn't changed.

00:17:01.990 --> 00:17:02.960
Indeed.

00:17:09.260 --> 00:17:14.040
It's as if we've time traveled 
back to the town from our memories.

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:19.360
You're a romantic, Mr. Llama.

00:17:19.890 --> 00:17:20.880
Am I?

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:40.200
Hama no Yu

00:17:37.620 --> 00:17:38.790
Miss Sasako,

00:17:38.790 --> 00:17:40.200
where are you?

00:17:40.870 --> 00:17:42.680
You were taking a while,

00:17:42.680 --> 00:17:44.660
so we decided to take a bath.

00:17:52.840 --> 00:17:55.120
That was a great bath.

00:17:55.720 --> 00:17:58.280
A hot bath is great once in a while.

00:17:58.710 --> 00:18:00.910
Isn't it nostalgic, Miss Sasako?

00:18:01.420 --> 00:18:03.090
Why don't you have a quick bath?

00:18:03.090 --> 00:18:04.910
No, I'm fine...

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:10.400
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:18:14.590 --> 00:18:17.870
So you still can't remember 
what you buried?

00:18:18.310 --> 00:18:19.320
Indeed.

00:18:19.980 --> 00:18:21.530
Maybe it was a clay figure.

00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:25.290
I bet 10,000 tugrik that it's not.

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:27.670
It's gotta be point cards!

00:18:28.600 --> 00:18:30.750
I think they might have expired...

00:18:31.190 --> 00:18:32.620
Buried treasure.

00:18:33.480 --> 00:18:35.460
You're thinking of Tokugawa.

00:18:36.960 --> 00:18:38.690
My heart is beating fast.

00:18:39.790 --> 00:18:41.930
We're almost there, everyone.

00:18:42.480 --> 00:18:44.150
As soon as we turn the corner...

00:18:44.150 --> 00:18:45.390
It's the Mononoke Forest.

00:18:54.080 --> 00:18:57.620
Probably not going to be able to 
dig up the time capsule now.

00:18:58.860 --> 00:19:01.410
Looks like they left the cedar.

00:19:01.410 --> 00:19:03.450
I buried it under there...

00:19:10.030 --> 00:19:12.250
I'm hungry.

00:19:13.210 --> 00:19:14.310
Would you like some bread?

00:19:20.630 --> 00:19:22.250
It's delicious!

00:19:22.700 --> 00:19:24.910
The simplicity of the taste is great.

00:19:25.330 --> 00:19:27.680
There's a lot of custard 
cream in it, isn't there?

00:19:28.470 --> 00:19:30.400
The taste hasn't changed at all.

00:19:34.090 --> 00:19:36.320
What? Do you see Superman?

00:19:37.140 --> 00:19:38.140
No.

00:19:39.600 --> 00:19:40.440
Look.

00:19:40.440 --> 00:19:42.410
You can see the windmill, right?

00:19:43.570 --> 00:19:46.270
That's a very memorable 
windmill to me.

00:19:50.910 --> 00:19:53.420
It's too bad though, Mr. Llama.

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:54.740
Indeed.

00:19:55.480 --> 00:19:59.800
But it was great just being 
able to come back here.

00:20:00.560 --> 00:20:02.050
Oh, I know.

00:20:02.050 --> 00:20:02.950
What?

00:20:06.860 --> 00:20:09.140
Hello! Sorry for taking so long.

00:20:09.710 --> 00:20:12.110
We're counting on you, Badger.

00:20:12.110 --> 00:20:14.380
Leave digging holes to me!

00:20:14.380 --> 00:20:15.960
It's right under the cedar.

00:20:16.620 --> 00:20:18.010
Thank you very much.

00:20:18.010 --> 00:20:19.150
Okay!

00:20:21.240 --> 00:20:30.250
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:20:26.300 --> 00:20:30.250
To future 
Llama

00:20:34.270 --> 00:20:35.670
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:20:36.250 --> 00:20:37.270
Did you find it?

00:20:37.270 --> 00:20:38.830
Tokugawa's buried treasure?

00:20:39.290 --> 00:20:42.760
I'm sure Mr. Itoi would be 
disappointed if it was found.

00:20:43.110 --> 00:20:44.620
Mr. Mizuno, too.

00:20:45.110 --> 00:20:47.660
Mr. Itoi? Mr. Mizuno?

00:20:48.110 --> 00:20:50.820
It's useless knowledge, Panda.

00:20:51.930 --> 00:20:57.610
To future Llama

00:20:52.430 --> 00:20:53.560
Is this it?

00:20:54.310 --> 00:20:55.050
Yes!

00:20:55.730 --> 00:20:57.610
I wonder what's inside.

00:21:04.380 --> 00:21:05.720
What's that?

00:21:06.280 --> 00:21:08.020
A cassette tape?

00:21:12.960 --> 00:21:14.210
Thanks for your hard work.

00:21:15.110 --> 00:21:18.670
Here's some pasta with cream sauce,
 with seasonal mushrooms.

00:21:19.590 --> 00:21:20.450
Eat up.

00:21:20.450 --> 00:21:22.010
I love mushrooms!

00:21:22.010 --> 00:21:23.170
Thank you for the food!

00:21:23.910 --> 00:21:26.030
What's recorded on here?

00:21:26.440 --> 00:21:28.210
It's probably Shinshou's 
traditional storytelling.

00:21:28.210 --> 00:21:29.820
It's not traditional story telling.

00:21:30.390 --> 00:21:31.810
Then what is it?

00:21:33.600 --> 00:21:35.620
We'll just have to listen and see.

00:21:36.670 --> 00:21:39.310
Is this it, Mr. Polar Bear?

00:21:39.780 --> 00:21:42.520
Thanks. I'm surprised you found it.

00:21:47.080 --> 00:21:49.060
Okay, here goes.

00:21:55.410 --> 00:21:58.560
<i>Llama ma ma, llama ma ma, 
llama ma ma ma...</i>

00:21:58.560 --> 00:21:59.460
<i>Llamambo!</i>

00:21:59.460 --> 00:22:02.400
<i>Llama ma ma, llama ma ma, 
llama ma ma ma...</i>

00:22:01.580 --> 00:22:03.270
What is this?

00:22:02.400 --> 00:22:03.270
<i>Llamambo!</i>

00:22:03.270 --> 00:22:05.940
It's a song I wrote.

00:22:05.940 --> 00:22:10.370
They called me the Third Avenue 
Mozart when I was a kid.

00:22:12.100 --> 00:22:14.230
Wow. Amazing.

00:22:15.760 --> 00:22:18.590
Could I get another café 
mocha, Polar Bear?

00:23:54.830 --> 00:24:25.250
Next Time

00:23:58.230 --> 00:23:59.880
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:23:59.880 --> 00:24:01.030
What is it, Panda?

00:24:01.030 --> 00:24:04.210
When do you think I'll get a 
subsidy for my cuteness?

00:24:04.210 --> 00:24:06.070
Don't think you ever will.

00:24:06.070 --> 00:24:07.800
Okay, then I'll give you 200 yen,

00:24:07.800 --> 00:24:09.050
so could you give me 
20,000 yen in return?

00:24:09.050 --> 00:24:12.470
I don't think anyone on Earth 
would say yes to that trade.

00:24:12.470 --> 00:24:14.970
How are red bean soup
 and red-bean soup different?

00:24:14.970 --> 00:24:16.510
We can discuss that later.

00:24:16.510 --> 00:24:18.100
Let's end this, Polar Bear.

00:24:18.330 --> 00:24:20.680
Next week's Polar Bear 
Café 24 o'clock...

00:24:20.680 --> 00:24:23.060
Not gonna even announce the 
last episode correctly, huh?

00:24:21.430 --> 00:24:24.910
Mr. Penguin's Secret
Cherry Blossom Viewing in Spring

00:24:23.060 --> 00:24:24.090
Enjoy!
